  "instructions": "HTML, CSS and JavaScript graded practical (Day S27). One 120-minute build on a fresh scenario, distinct from the Trail Guides practice labs and modestly harder than them, limited to taught content. The sitting begins by scaffolding a new Vite project with npm and starting its development server; the learner then builds into it, from provided data and a provided running REST API: an accessible, responsive page that loads the API's data, renders it safely, updates it through a validated form, handles network and ProblemDetail error paths, and includes at least one pure function with its own Vitest test. The four modules weigh equally (see weights). Standard-track learners receive fuller setup guidance in the task sheet; Fast-track learners receive the same tasks with leaner scaffolding; the blueprint, tasks and scoring weights are identical for both tracks. The 120-minute duration is a planning allowance, not a piloted measurement: the platform assessment owner may trim the task set per sitting while keeping the stated weights. Graded task text, data and scoring material are platform-owned and are not published in this repository. The pass mark is 70%."
